{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "טמא לנפש", :translit "tamei la-nefesh", :gloss "unclean by reason of a corpse"} {:he "טמא", :translit "tamei", :gloss "unclean"} {:he "לנפש", :translit "la-nefesh", :gloss "by reason of a corpse"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Paseq (vertical bar) between טמא and לנפש signals a halakhic distinction: individual displaced from Pesach, congregation not."}], :frame {:text "The paseq is a cantillation mark consisting of a vertical bar separating two words. Its presence here is read as hermeneutically significant, indicating a distinction in the laws of impurity as they relate to Pesach Sheni: an individual who is tamei is displaced from offering the Pesach and must bring it in the second month, but if the entire congregation is tamei, they are not displaced (Pesachim 79a).", :sources ["Pesachim 79a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "או בדרך רחוקה", :translit "o va-derech rechoqah", :gloss "or on a journey far off"} {:he "רחוקה", :translit "rechoqah", :gloss "far off"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "רחוקה", :b "זהו"}], :frame {:text "The Ba'al HaTurim notes a gematria equivalence between רחוקה and זהו, and draws attention to the masoretic dot markings on the letters of או בדרך רחקה in Numbers 9:10. The rabbis interpret these dotted letters to limit the definition of a distant journey (Pesachim 93b).", :sources ["Numbers 9:10" "Pesachim 93b"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ועשה פסח לה' בחודש השני", :translit "ve-asah pesach la-Shem be-chodesh ha-sheini", :gloss "and they shall keep the Passover to YHWH in the second month"}], :mechanisms [], :frame {:text "The second month (Iyar) substitutes for Nisan when the year is intercalated (Sanhedrin 11b). The manna began falling on the fifteenth of Iyar, the day after the Israelites' provisions from Egypt were exhausted; according to tradition this fell on a Sunday (Shabbat 87b).", :sources ["Sanhedrin 11b" "Shabbat 87b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Paseq (vertical bar) between טמא and לנפש signals a halakhic distinction: individual displaced from Pesach, congregation not.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "רחוקה", :a-value 319, :b "זהו", :b-value 18, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:27:56.546425460Z", :model "glm-5.2"}